cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Real-time-middleware: a C++ reimplementation of the MCFlow multi-core real-time middleware"
abstract: >-
  C++17 reimplementation of the MCFlow middleware for dependent task graphs on
  multi-core platforms, extended with configurable bin-packing core allocation
  (First Fit, Best Fit, Worst Fit, with period and utilization sort criteria)
  and a measurement harness that reports per-job scheduling latency, jitter and
  deadline misses under SCHED_FIFO on Linux PREEMPT_RT.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Onofre de Oliveira"
    given-names: "Tassany"
    email: "tassany.onofre-de-oliveira@enac.fr"
    affiliation: "ENAC - Ecole Nationale de l'Aviation Civile, Toulouse, France"
    # TODO: uncomment and fill in before submitting the article.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tassany/Real-time-middleware"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - real-time systems
  - middleware
  - multi-core scheduling
  - task graph
  - bin packing
  - SCHED_FIFO
  - PREEMPT_RT
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "MCFlow: a Real-time Multi-core Aware Middleware for Dependent Task Graphs"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Huang"
        given-names: "Huang-Ming"
      - family-names: "Gill"
        given-names: "Christopher"
      - family-names: "Lu"
        given-names: "Chenyang"
    collection-title: "2012 IEEE International Conference on Embedded and Real-Time Computing Systems and Applications (RTCSA)"
    year: 2012
    notes: "Reference paper reimplemented by this software."

